    "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the current ages of Alex and Allison based on the information given about Diane's age and the relationships between their ages.\n\n1. **Determine Diane's age in 30 years:**\n   Diane will be 30 years old when she turns 30. Since she is currently 16 years old, in 30 years she will be:\n   \\[\n   16 + 30 = 46 \\text{ years old}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Set up the equations based on the relationships given:**\n   - When Diane is 30, she will be half the age of Alex. Let Alex's current age be \\( A \\). Then:\n     \\[\n     30 = \\frac{A}{2} \\implies A = 60\n     \\]\n   - When Diane is 30, she will be twice as old as Allison. Let Allison's current age be \\( L \\). Then:\n     \\[\n     30 = 2L \\implies L = 15\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the sum of the ages of Alex and Allison:**\n   The sum of Alex's and Allison's current ages is:\n   \\[\n   A + L = 60 + 15 = 75\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the ages of Alex and Allison now is \\(\\boxed{75}\\).",
